# Visual refresh handoff

## Every chat

1. At the start, read `design/HANDOFF.md`.
2. Do any **OPEN** items addressed **to Cursor**. Do not wait for Nathan to repeat them.
3. At the end of the chat (or when you finish those items), add a newest-at-top log entry: date, from Cursor, to (Jam / Pixel / Nathan), status, what you did, files.

Entry shape (copy this):

```
## YYYY-MM-DD — short title
- From: Cursor
- To: Jam / Pixel / Nathan
- Status: OPEN | DONE | BLOCKED
- What:
- Files:
```

## Do not

- Do not rewrite `data/player-copy.json` text (or author-locked board/catalog copy). Flag problems in HANDOFF instead.
- Player screens never show the word **Tier**. They show Weak / Tough / Deadly.
- Do not restyle or redesign the game until a `design/visual/specs/SCREEN-*.md` build spec (from Pixel) is OPEN to Cursor.
